 **Start here:** [November 17 results and proposal task ledger (Chinese)](docs/PROPOSAL_RESULTS_2026-11-17.zh.md), [complete English research report](report/report.md), [reproduction and local delivery](research/proposal_completion_20261117/REPRODUCE.md), and [pipeline commands](benchmark/physcheck/relations/README.md). The [November 16 summary](docs/PROJECT_SUMMARY_2026-11-16.zh.md) and [historical index](research/project_summary_20261116/EXPERIMENT_INDEX.md) retain the preceding state.
 
 **Proposal closeout:** the earlier 325-input matrix is retained. All 30 DAVIS clips/650 queries were freshly inferred through the unified CLI and reproduced the baseline. The same three PStudio videos now use all 150 frames: Co+depth lacks 85/1,848 required point-times (full EPE N/A), while TAPIP3D full macro EPE is 52.88 cm. A local pinned Qwen visual judge obtained 2/12 correct gravity controls and 4/8 human-PC calibration cases; its separate 8/16 test result is diagnostic only. Four old I2V clips received isolated visual opinions, but usable physical validation remains unmet. That closeout recorded **117 passing tests**; the newer experiment below records the current suite. These are reruns/extensions and scoped probes, not new independent generator samples.
 
-**Latest measurement experiment:** a [frozen EgoPoints pilot](research/real_measurement_20261117/report/REPORT.zh.md) used 12 new real sequences, 10 participant groups and 119 queries. Reciprocal verification reached 95.83% accepted precision with 44.66% correct retention, while reappearance recovery fell from 12/16 to 4/16. Its empirical gate passes on this small sample, with a 90.20%–100% descriptive precision interval; it is not a production identity-recovery upgrade. CUDA cache management corrected execution from 7/12 to 12/12 with identical arrays on all seven earlier successes. The workspace suite now has 123 passing tests. See [reproduction](research/real_measurement_20261117/REPRODUCE.md) and [remaining limits](research/real_measurement_20261117/FAILURES_AND_LIMITS.md).
+**Latest measurement experiment:** the [frozen reference-matching comparison](research/reference_relocalization_20261117/report_v2/REPORT.zh.md) added three participant-disjoint, human-labeled EgoPoints sequences: 1,051 frames and 27 queries. Native CoTracker3 localized 28/42 known visible point-times correctly; static MASt3R localized 21/42, adding zero correct positions and losing seven. Accepted precision was 82.76% versus 51.22% for MASt3R reciprocity. Its single added accepted return already had a correct native coordinate. The official PointSt3R weight link expired, so this is explicitly a public MASt3R baseline, not a PointSt3R replication. The workspace suite has **130 passing tests**.
+
+The same frozen CoTracker reverse gate reached 93.75% precision with 35.71% correct retention on the new sample. Ten of twelve return events came from one participant, and there were no occluded negatives; no production upgrade or population false-positive bound follows. See [new-case diagnostics](research/reference_relocalization_20261117/VALIDATION_DIAGNOSTICS.zh.md), [reproduction](research/reference_relocalization_20261117/REPRODUCE.md), and [preserved failures](research/reference_relocalization_20261117/FAILURES_AND_LIMITS.md). Native tracking remains the reference while explicit visibility and identity recovery remain open.
+
+**Previous measurement round (development data for the comparison above):** the [EgoPoints pilot](research/real_measurement_20261117/report/REPORT.zh.md) used 12 real sequences, 10 participant groups and 119 queries. Reciprocal verification reached 95.83% accepted precision with 44.66% correct retention, while accepted reappearance recovery fell from 12/16 to 4/16. Its empirical gate passed on that small sample, with a 90.20%–100% descriptive precision interval; it was not a production identity-recovery upgrade. CUDA cache management corrected execution from 7/12 to 12/12 with identical arrays on all seven earlier successes. That round recorded 123 passing tests.
 
 The earlier action-conditioned linear-state pilot remains a completed historical side study; its visual/latent-model continuation has not been implemented. The previous README is preserved with the summary's source snapshots.
 
